    "ticket.comments": "",
    "ticket.description": "# eh run: reserved exit codes for eh-detected failure categories\n\n## Problem\n\n`eh run` collapses distinct failures into indistinguishable exit codes: a missing harness binary (spawn `ENOENT`), a semantic harness failure (`resultIsError` with child exit 0), and preflight errors all become `1`, while raw child codes pass through. An orchestrator supervising many lanes cannot classify a dead lane (retry? reconfigure? report?) without parsing stderr.\n\n## Context\n\n* Branch from `origin/main` (local main is 7 commits behind).\n* Current derivation lives in `executePreparedHeadlessPlan` (`src/headless-run.ts` ~lines 246–272: `completed.code ?? (signalNumber ? 128 + signalNumber : 1)`, `resultIsError` forcing `1`, spawn-error path) and the preflight catch in `runHeadless` (~lines 105–108).\n* Decision (made with repo owner): eh owns a small reserved, documented, contiguous exit-code block at ≥64; raw harness codes pass through unchanged when eh has no better category; `run.completed.exitCode` keeps meaning \"the raw child exit code\". Provider/auth-error classification is explicitly deferred — it requires per-harness error-shape parsing.\n* The existing test \"emits a run error when a harness exits non-zero without a semantic error\" expects raw passthrough (`7`) and must stay green — this test staying green unmodified is the proof for the passthrough invariant below.\n* The `--cwd` and `--timeout` tickets touch the same region of `headless-run.ts`. Land serially — suggested order: cwd, timeout, then this ticket.\n* Accepted limitation (documentable, not fixable here): a timed-out run and any other SIGTERM'd run both surface as `128+15` — orchestrators that need to distinguish them read the `run.error` event.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] eh-detected categories exit with distinct documented codes from one reserved contiguous block at ≥64 (exact numbers implementer's choice, recorded in the README table): at minimum spawn failure (binary missing/unspawnable), semantic harness failure (`resultIsError` with child exit 0), and preflight/usage errors (TTY or empty stdin, invalid flag values). Clean completion remains 0. Proof: extend the existing missing-binary / semantic-failure / preflight subprocess tests to assert the reserved codes.\n- [ ] Invariant: a raw child exit code is never remapped when eh has no category for the failure — the existing nonzero-passthrough and `128 + signal` behaviors are unchanged, and `run.completed.exitCode` continues to carry the raw child code (its field semantics do not change).\n- [ ] README gains an \"Exit codes\" table (mirrored in DESIGN.md's headless section) documenting the reserved block, the passthrough rule, and the caveat that a harness's own code may numerically collide with the reserved block only in the passthrough case.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n* Provider/auth-error classification (deferred by decision — per-harness error-shape parsing).\n* An `errorCategory` field on `run.completed` (may come later; exit codes are the contract for now).\n* Timeout's exit code: if the `--timeout` ticket has landed, its `128 + signal` shape may optionally be documented in the table, but remapping it is not required here.\n\n## Verification\n\n* `pnpm lint:ci`; `bun test src/headless-run.test.ts`; full `pnpm test`.\n* Version bump required; update README, DESIGN.md, `docs/qa/eh-cli.md`.\n\n## Delegability\n\n```yaml\ndesign_freedom: medium\nverification_strength: high\nsilent_failure_cost: medium\ncontext_volatility: low\nrecommended_tier: medium\nrecommended_effort: medium\n```",
